# Docker build-context excludes. The Dockerfile does `COPY . ${ROS_WS}/`, so
# anything left here is both streamed to the daemon AND baked into the image
# layer. Keep only what the image needs to build the colcon overlay and run the
# in-image tests (src/, entrypoint.sh, requirements.txt). Everything below is
# host-only dev cruft — excluding it removed ~314 MB from the image (the COPY
# layer went from 316 MB to ~2 MB) and shrinks the context transfer on rebuild.

# Local Python virtualenv (~291 MB) — the image uses apt/system Python, never .venv.
.venv/

# Git history & tooling metadata — not needed at runtime.
.git/
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# Lint / test / coverage caches (host-side, regenerated).
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Docs & media (docs/media holds a multi-MB demo recording) — not shipped.
docs/

# colcon build artifacts, if a local build ever left them: they would clash with
# the in-image `colcon build` and pull stale symlinks into the image.
build/
install/
log/

# Python bytecode / packaging artifacts.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
